{"id": "EUVD-2026-97432", "enisaUuid": "91c69b55-47ed-3533-841c-0beacd76e3da", "description": "SGLang through 0.5.21 contains a decompression amplification vulnerability in load_audio that allows remote attackers to exhaust memory by submitting highly compressed audio decoded without duration or sample limits. Attackers can supply small FLAC-encoded silence files through audio_url or audio_data inputs that expand into massive PCM buffers, exhausting worker memory and CPU for denial of service.", "datePublished": "2026-10-12T14:04:30", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-13T18:24:26", "baseScore": 8.7, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:N/VI:N/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/issues/43708", "https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/v0.5.21/python/sglang/srt/utils/common.py#L1783", "https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/v0.5.21/python/sglang/srt/utils/common.py#L1801-L1803", "https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/v0.5.21/python/sglang/srt/multimodal/audio_from_video.py#L128", "https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/v0.5.21/python/sglang/srt/multimodal/processors/base_processor.py#L996", "https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/sglang-through-0.5.21-audio-decompression-amplification-via-load-audio"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-109226", "GHSA-h3xf-3226-h48g"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.46, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "2d4cff05-37d2-377e-b304-036ea8a62f04", "product": {"name": "sglang", "vendor": {"name": "sgl-project"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22640.5.21"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "3ec08004-69ca-3700-a6ed-adf927e80ee8", "vendor": {"name": "sgl-project"}}], "isExploited": false}